triage: fix_game: Every failure is a presentation slip in the file, not a problem with the rules or the platform. Prompts use placeholders the step cannot fill ({decl_value}, {decl_cards}), and internal scratch attributes (decl_answer, drawn_hidden_card, follow_card, led_card) are left visible. The coder has been fixing one of these and reintroducing the other, so both must be fixed together.
step C: building the game file
triage: revise_rules: Over four attempts the coder has swung between the same two failures: empty internal fields in the shown state, and the declaration bookkeeping (declared_this_deal, declared_cards_shown, decl_value, decl_cards) never firing in random matches. The declaration is gated by several conditions at once (won the previous trick, not yet declared, holds a qualifying three-of-rank or Napoli, chooses to declare), so it is both rarely reached and hard to detect with flat arithmetic steps over a hand. The interface also requires a public `talon_up` that is legitimately empty for half of every deal.
